cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "From Crypt Base to Villus Tip: an interactive 3D model of an intestinal epithelial cell's journey"
message: >-
  If you use this model, please cite both the archived software record
  and the associated review.
type: software
abstract: >-
  An interactive three-dimensional model that follows one intestinal epithelial
  cell from the stem-cell niche at the crypt base to its extrusion at the villus
  tip, showing the changes in cell shape, force and signalling along the
  crypt-villus axis. A cut-away overview of a villus and its crypts is paired
  with a close-up section of the followed cell and its neighbours, and colour
  modes show actomyosin, traction, Wnt/BMP, EphB/ephrin-B, enterocyte zones,
  migration speed and Confetti lineage tracing. Statements are tagged by their
  evidence (tissue, organoid, preprint, or the review's own model). A schematic
  teaching model that runs offline in any browser.
keywords:
  - intestine
  - crypt-villus axis
  - intestinal stem cells
  - cell extrusion
  - epithelial mechanics
  - cell migration
  - lineage tracing
  - interactive model
